# Append-only files use git's union merge driver.
#
# These are logs, not documents: every writer appends, nobody edits earlier
# entries. A textual 3-way merge treats two branches appending at the same
# offset as a conflict, which it isn't — union keeps both sides' lines.
#
# The dejavue block below was previously present twice, verbatim; deduped
# 2026-07-24.
.dejavue/timeline.jsonl   merge=union
.dejavue/decisions.md     merge=union
.dejavue/invariants.md    merge=union
.dejavue/patterns.md      merge=union

# The planning backlog is appended to by every agent that runs `dejavue plan`
# (capture-on-discovery), so it conflicts on exactly the same pattern as the
# dejavue logs — but was never covered. Added 2026-07-24 after it conflicted
# on two separate branches in a single cleanup pass.
.jagent/planning/TASKS.md merge=union
